= USPD Party Conference

Now is the USPD's national party conference, where they will choose their new leadership. The shadow of the Wittorf Affair hangs over it. On one hand are the Spartacist supporters of Liebknecht, who support a more cooperative policy towards the SPD. On the other hand is the Communist faction, who support a "social fascist" policy that places the SPD as equivalent to the Nazis.

After our discussion with the Soviets, we are inclined to believe that Stalin is at least open to a continued Liebknecht Chairmanship. In order to affect the USPD's leadership elections, we have to influence both the Comintern leaders as as well as the USPD membership.

- @liebknecht_lives_on
- @communists_triumphant


@liebknecht_lives_on
title: Karl Liebknecht successfully defends the Charimanship!
choose-if: (left_strength >= reformist_strength) and (uspd_relation >= 50) 
unavailable-subtitle: [?  if not levi_advisor and not rosenfeld_advisor: Our party leadership is not left-wing enough. ?] [? if left_strength < reformist_strength: The Comintern doubts our commitment to socialism. ?]
on-arrival: uspd_party_leader = "Luxemburgists"; spartacist_coalition += 3; uspd_relation += 10*(1-dissent); left_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 8
achievement: versohnler

With our support, Karl Liebknecht has won the leadership contest! We hope, with his position secured, that Liebknecht will be more inclined towards continued and further cooperation.


@communists_triumphant
title: Ernst Thälmann wins the Chairmanship!

Unfortunately, we could not influence the USPD leadership election against the hardliners and the Communists emerge triumphant. Thälmann quickly moves to consolidate absolute leadership, expelling or exiling his opponents, and reforms the party into the KPD.
